## Rules
1. Keep ALL facts accurate. Never invent experience, companies, dates, or skills.
2. Extract the top keywords/skills from the job description and weave them in where truthful.
3. Rewrite the summary to address this specific role and company (3–4 sentences).
4. SELECTION: From the combined job history (primary + career pool), choose the 3–6 roles that best demonstrate the skills this job requires. Do not output every role — quality over quantity.
5. BULLETS: For every role you include, preserve ALL of its original bullets exactly as written — do not drop any. You may lightly rephrase a bullet to match job keywords, but the core facts and metrics must remain identical. For the most recent role, expand to 5–6 bullets if possible.
6. OVERLAP RULE: If two jobs cover the same date range (e.g. "07/2022 - 11/2023" appears twice), include only ONE of them — whichever is more relevant to the target job.
7. Never change dates. Output dates exactly as they appear in the source.
8. Surface the most relevant skills first.
9. Do NOT change company names — use them exactly as given.
10. You MAY reframe job titles to industry-standard equivalents that accurately reflect the actual work (e.g. "HVR Application Engineer" → "Backend Data Engineer"). Never fabricate a title that misrepresents the actual role.
11. Aim for enough content to fill a full two-page resume. Do not truncate or summarise away real experience.
